pattern ^-?(?:0|[1-9]\d*)(?:\.\d+)?$
name base10num-near-miss
tag family=wild-logparse, hazard=none
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license n-a
  fidelity synthesized
  adaptation |
    the JSON-number grammar's leading-zero/bare-sign strictness (RFC 8259 §6); pairs against L1's imported grok BASE10NUM pattern named in capability_set_v1.md §3.1 family 1

pattern ^(?>(?:kern|user|mail|daemon|auth|syslog|cron)\.(?:emerg|alert|crit|err|warning|notice|info|debug)): (.*)$
name logparse-atomic
tag family=wild-logparse, hazard=exponential-backtracking, requires=atomic-group
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license n-a
  fidelity synthesized
  adaptation |
    modeled on grok's own SYSLOGFACILITY-style facility.severity tag matching (the family's cited wild source is grok's log macros, capability_set_v1.md §3.1 family 2); the atomic wrap follows the family's own stress-mechanism text verbatim: "atomic groups the ORIGINAL author added to fight backtracking"

pattern ^(?:(?:kern|user|mail|daemon|auth|syslog|cron)\.(?:emerg|alert|crit|err|warning|notice|info|debug)): (.*)$
name logparse-atomic-removed
tag family=wild-logparse, hazard=exponential-backtracking
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license n-a
  fidelity synthesized
  adaptation |
    the family's own designed-member spec verbatim: "the same pattern with the atomic groups REMOVED -- the author's own fix as a control pair" (capability_set_v1.md §3.1 family 2)

