name wild-logparse-syslogbase-expanded
tag family=wild-logparse, hazard=exponential-backtracking, requires=lookaround, requires=named-groups
provenance
  source grok
  url https://raw.githubusercontent.com/logstash-plugins/logstash-patterns-core/main/patterns/legacy/grok-patterns
  ref grok-patterns:92 (SYSLOGBASE) + its own transitive %{...} macros (SYSLOGTIMESTAMP:81, SYSLOGFACILITY:85, SYSLOGHOST:84/IPORHOST:32/IP:30/IPV6:28/IPV4:29/HOSTNAME:31, SYSLOGPROG:83/PROG:82, MONTH:51, MONTHDAY:54, TIME:65/HOUR:61/MINUTE:62/SECOND:64, NONNEGINT:12, POSINT:11)
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license Apache-2.0
  fidelity adapted
  adaptation |
    every %{NAME} and %{NAME:label} grok macro reference mechanically substituted, recursively, by the named pattern's own definition in the same file -- unlabelled to a plain non-capturing group (?:...), labelled to a named group (?<label>...), exactly grok's own compile step -- producing one self-contained pattern with no remaining %{...} references

